  "reason": "The key finding so far is that RNA-only (config_044, acc 0.5305) outperforms both multimodal configs (config_002 at 0.5251, config_006 at 0.5121), suggesting the image modality with resnet50 is not contributing positively. The most critical uncertainty is whether this is an inherent limitation of the image modality or specific to the resnet50 encoder. Config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) isolates exactly this variable: it is identical to the best multimodal result (config_002) except the image encoder is swapped from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l. If imagenet_vit_l also fails to beat RNA-only, we gain strong evidence that the image channel is unhelpful in this task and can focus remaining budget on RNA-side improvements. If it does close or reverse the gap, we identify the image encoder as the bottleneck and have a clear exploitation path. This single-variable comparison is the most information-dense next experiment under a limited budget."
}

